hadiths[64]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1322","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a pile of food. He put his fingers in it and felt wetness. He said: 'O owner of the food! What is this ?' He replied: 'It was rained upon O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Why not put it on top of the food so the people can see it?' Then he said: 'Whoever cheats"
"1323","Narrated Abu Hurairah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took a camel of a particular age on loan. He gave back to him a camel of a better age than the one he was given. He said: 'The best among you is the best in repaying.'\"" He said: There is something on this topic from Abu Rafi'. [Abu 'Eisa said:] The Hadith of Abu Hurairah is a Hasan Sahih Hadith. Shu'bah and Sufyan reported it from Salamah. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge"""""
"1324","Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) reported that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) prohibited *muḥāqalah*, *muzābanah*, *mukhābarah*, and *muʿāwamah*, and he granted a concession (rukhṣah) regarding *ʿarāyā*. Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.\n\nThe hadith, narrated by Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) and recorded by al-Tirmidhī, addresses several forms of agricultural and produce-related transactions that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) prohibited due to their inherent *gharar* (excessive uncertainty) and resemblance to *ribā* (usury). The prohibited terms are as follows:\n\n1. Al-Muḥāqalah (المحاقلة): Selling the wheat crop while still in the ears (i.e., grain still unthreshed) in exchange for threshed grain. This involves an uncertain measure, as the final yield is unknown.\n\n2. Al-Muzābanah (المزابنة): Selling unripe dates on the palm tree in exchange for dried (tamr) dates by estimation, without actual weighing or measuring after harvest.\n\n3. Al-Mukhābarah (المخابرة): A share-cropping arrangement where a landowner gives a plot to a cultivator in exchange for a portion of the yield, often involving ambiguity in the division.\n\n4. Al-Muʿāwamah (المعاومة): Selling fruit crops one or two years in advance before they materialize, a form of forward contract with excessive *gharar*.\n\nThe Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) granted a rukhṣah (concession) regarding *ʿarāyā*, which refers to the exchange of fresh dates on the tree for dried dates by estimation, specifically for a limited quantity (usually five *awsq* or less), to assist those in need. This exception is based on the hadith of Abū Hurayrah and others, where the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) allowed this transaction out of mercy and necessity, provided it is conducted fairly.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī (raḥimahullāh) classified this narration as ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ (good and authentic), affirming its reliability in Islamic jurisprudence."
"1325","for indeed the owner of the the right has the right to speak.' Then he said: 'Purchase a camel for him and give it to him.' So they searched out but they did not find a camel but of a better ager than his camel. So he said: 'Buy it and give it to him. For indeed the best of you is the best in repaying.' \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1317 Arabic Hadees: 1317\""1326"""""
"1326","‘Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us; Isma‘il ibn Ja‘far informed us; from al-‘Ala’ ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman; from his father; from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a heap of food. He put his hand into it, and his fingers touched moisture. He said: ""O owner of the food, what is this?"" He said: ""The rain fell on it, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Why did you not put it on top of the food so that people could see it?"" Then he said: ""Whoever deceives is not from us."" He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Ibn ‘Umar, Abu al-Hamra’, Ibn ‘Abbas, Buraydah, Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman. Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of Abu Hurayrah is Hasan Sahih. The practice upon this is among the people of knowledge: they disliked deception and said deception is haram."
"1327","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah loves tolerance in selling"""""
"1328","Narrated Jabir: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah forgave a man who was before you: He was tolerant when selling"""""
"1329","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you see someone selling or buying in the Masjid then say: 'May Allah not profit your business.' And when you see someone announcing about something lost then say: 'May Allah not return it to you.'\"" The Hadith of Abu Hurairah is Hasan Gharib. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. They dislike selling and buying in the Masjid. This is the view of Ahmad and Ishaq. Some of the people of knowledge permitted selling and buying in the Masjid"""""
"1330","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (sallAllahu Alayhi wa sallam) said:\Whoever asks for a position as a judge"""""
"1331","Anas narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\Whoever seeks to be a judge"""""
"1332","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\Whoever takes the responsibility of judge"""""
"1333","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\When the judge passes a judgement in which he strived and was correct"""""
"1334","Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakrah narrated:""My father wrote to 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Bakrah who was a judge: ""Do not pass a judgement between two people while you are angry, for indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'The judge should not judge between two people while he is angry"
"1335","Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakrah narrated:\My father wrote to 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Bakrah who was a judge: \""Do not pass a judgement between two people while you are angry"""""
"1336","Mu'adh bin Jabal narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched me to Yemen. When I had left"""""
"1337","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the one who bribes and the one who takes a bribe for a judgement"""""
"1338","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the one who bribes and the one who takes a bribe"""""
"1339","Anas bin Malik narrated that Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\If trotter (lacking meat) were given to me I would accept it"""""
"1340","Umm Salamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\Indeed you come to me with your disputes"""""
"1341","Alqamah bin Wa'il [bin Hujr] narrated from his father who said:\A man from Hadramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Prophet (ﷺ). The Hadrami said: 'O Messenger of Allah! This person took some land of mine.' The Kindi said:'It is my land"""""
"1342","Narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Kūfī — Muhammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us, from Fuḍayl ibn Marzūq, from 'Aṭiyyah, from Abū Sa'īd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\n> The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: *\Indeed"
"1343","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that the oath is due from the one the claim is made against"
"1344","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with one witness.\"" Rabi'ah (one of the narrators) said: \""A son of Ibn Sa'd bin 'Ubadah informed me saying: 'We found in a book of Sa'd that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with a witness"""""
"1345","Jabir narrated:\The Prophet (ﷺ) passed judgement based on oath along with a witness"""""
"1346","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father:\The Prophet (ﷺ) passed judgement based on an oath along with one witness.\"" He said: \""And 'Ali judged between you based on it"""""
"1347","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\Whoever frees a portion\"" or"""""
"1348","Salim narrated from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\Whoever frees a portion of a slave he owns"""""
"1349","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\Whoever frees a portion\"" or he said: \""a part of a slave"""""
"1350","Samurah narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\The lifelong gift is permitted for its inhabitant\"" or:\""is an inheritance for its inhabitant"""""
"1351","Jabir narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\Whichever man is given a lifelong gift for himself and his offspring"""""
"1352","Jabir narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\The lifelong gift is permitted for its inhabitant"""""
"1353","Qutaybah narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, from his father, who said:\n\nA man from Ḥaḍramawt and a man from Kindah came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Ḥaḍramī said, \O Messenger of Allah ﷺ"
"1354","Narrated by Ali ibn Hujr, who reported from Ali ibn Mushir and others, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, from Amr ibn Shu'aib, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ said in his sermon:\n\n\The burden of proof lies upon the claimant"
"1355","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The oath is based upon what will make your companion believe you.” [Qutaibah (one of the narrators) said: “ What will make you believed by your companion”"
"1356","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Make the road seven forearm lengths.”"
"1357","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\When you disagree over the road"""""
"1358","Abu Maimunah narrated from Abu Hurairah who said:\The Prophet (ﷺ) gave a boy the choice between his father and his mother"""""
"1359","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\Indeed the most wholesome of what you consume is from your earnings"""""
"1360","Anas narrated:\One of the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ) gave the Prophet (ﷺ) some food in a bowl. Then 'Aishah broke the bowl with her hand"""""
"1361","‘Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us; ‘Isa ibn Yunus informed us; from Sa‘id ibn Abi ‘Aroubah; from Qatadah; from al-Nadr ibn Anas; from Bashir ibn Nahik; from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever frees a share—or he said a portion (shiqs)—in a slave, his complete emancipation is (binding) upon his wealth if he has wealth. If he has no wealth, the slave is valued at a fair price, then the slave works (yusta‘sa) for the share that was not freed, without overburdening him."" He said: In this chapter there is a narration from ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Amr. Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa‘id narrated to us; from Sa‘id ibn Abi ‘Aroubah, similarly, and he said: ""shiqs."" Abu ‘Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith. And thus Aban ibn Yazid narrated from Qatadah, like the narration of Sa‘id ibn Abi ‘Aroubah. Shu‘bah narrated this hadith from Qatadah, but did not mention the matter of ‘sa‘yah (working for freedom). The people of knowledge differed regarding ‘sa‘yah. Some saw ‘sa‘yah in this, and this is the saying of Sufyan al-Thawri and the people of Kufa, and this is the saying of Ishaq. Some people of knowledge said: If a slave is owned by two men and one frees his share, if he has wealth, he is liable for his partner's share and the slave is freed from his wealth. If he has no wealth, the slave is freed to the extent of his share, and no ‘sa‘yah is imposed. They argued with what was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ). This is the saying of the people of Madinah, and this is the saying of Malik ibn Anas, al-Shafi‘i, and Ahmad."
"1362","Narrated Nafi':that Ibn 'Umar said: \I was reviewed before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the army"""""
"1363","Narrated Al-Bara':\My maternal uncle Abu Burdah Ibn Niyar passed by me and he had a flag with him. I said: 'Where are you going ?' He said: 'the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched me to a man who married a woman his father had married to: that I should bring him his head"""""
"1364","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:\A man from the Ansar disputed with Az-Zubair before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the canals of Harrah which they used to irrigate the date palms. The Ansari said: 'Let the water pass'. But he refused"""""
"1365","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:\A Man from the Ansar freed six slaves of his upon his death"""""
"1366","Sa‘īd ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ‘Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from al-A‘raj, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When one of you seeks permission from his neighbour to fix a wooden beam in his wall, he should not refuse him.” When Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrated this, they bowed their heads. He said: “What is the matter with you? Why do you turn away from it? By Allāh, I will surely cast it between your shoulders.” He said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Ibn ‘Abbās and Mujammi‘ ibn Jāriyah. Abū ‘Īsā said: The hadith of Abū Hurayrah is a hasan sahīh hadith. This is acted upon according to some of the scholars, and this is the view of al-Shāfi‘ī. It has been narrated from some of the scholars, including Mālik ibn Anas, that he said: He may prevent his neighbour from placing his beam in his wall. The first opinion is more correct."
"1367","Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:That his father gave a slave to a son of his. So he went to the Prophet (ﷺ) to have him witness it. He (ﷺ) said: 'Have you given a gift similar to this one to all of your sons?' He replied: 'No'. So he said: 'Then take him back"
"1368","Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Waki‘ narrated to us; from al-Muthanna ibn Sa‘id al-Duba‘i; from Qatadah; from Bashir ibn Nahik; from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Make the road seven cubits (adhru‘) wide."""""
"1369","Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:That his father gave a slave to a son of his. So he went to the Prophet (ﷺ) to have him witness it. He (ﷺ) said: 'Have you given a gift similar to this one to all of your sons?' He replied: 'No'. So he said: 'Then take him back"
"1370","Narrated Samurah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The neighbor of a home has more right to the home"""""
"1371","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The neighbor has more right to his preemption. He is to be waited for even if he is absent"""""
"1372","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the boundaries are defined and the streets are fixed"""""
"1373","Narrated Ibn Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The partner is the preemptor"""""
"1374","Narrated Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhni:\A man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about lost items. So he said: 'Make a public announcement about it for one year. Remember its string"""""
"1375","Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhni narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about the lost item. He said:\Make a public announcement about it for one year"""""
"1376","Suwaid bin Ghafalah said:\I went out with Zaid bin Suhan and Salman bin Rabi'ah"""""
"1377","Qutaybah narrated to us: Hammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه that a man from the Anṣār freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, and he had no other wealth besides them. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he spoke to him in severe terms. Then he called for the slaves, divided them into lots, and cast lots among them. He freed two and retained four.\n\nIt has been narrated through other chains from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه.\n\nHe (al-Tirmidhī) said: In this chapter there is also (a narration) from Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: The ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* ḥadīth.\n\nThe practice according to this is held by some of the people of knowledge from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others. It is the position of Mālik, al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq, who held the view of employing the casting of lots (*al-qurʿah*) in this matter and in other matters.\n\nAs for some of the people of knowledge from the people of Kūfah and others, they did not approve of the casting of lots and said: one-third of each slave should be freed, and the slave should be required to work to earn the remaining two-thirds of his value.\n\nAbū al-Muhallab's name is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Jarmī, and he is not Abū Qilābah. He is also called Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr. Abū Qilābah al-Jarmī's name is ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd."
"1378","Narrated Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever possesses a mahram relative"
"1379","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The injuries caused by the animal are without liability"""""
"1380","Narrated Sa'eed bin Zaid:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives a barren land then it is for him"""""
"1381","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives a barren land"""""
"1382","Narrated Shumair:that Abyad bin Hammal visited the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who asked him to set aside a reserve of salt(a mine). So he reserved it for him. As he was turning away"
"1383","Narrated 'Alqamah bin Wa'il:from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) set aside a land reserve for him in Hadramawt. (One of the narrators added): \And he sent Mu'awiyah with him to reserve it for him"""""
"1384","Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \No Muslim plants a plant or sows a crop"""""
"1385","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\The Prophet (ﷺ) made a deal with the people of Khaibar for half of what was produced from it"""""
